The user is showing a Zenodo error about the grant ID format. The error says `"Invalid value 00k4n6c32::10.13039/501100001659."` - this is related to the grants field in `.zenodo.json`.

Let me look at the current grants in the `.zenodo.json`:

```json
"grants": [
    {
      "id": "10.13039/501100001659",
      "title": "Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG) - Underlying research"
    },
    {
      "id": "info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/EC/H2020/101045376",
      "title": "European Research Council (ERC) - COSE (grant No. 101045376) - Underlying research"
    }
  ],
```

The problem is that Zenodo's grants field needs to reference specific grant agreements from OpenAIRE, not just funder DOIs. The first entry uses the DFG funder DOI instead of an actual grant ID, which is why Zenodo is rejecting it. I need to either find the proper OpenAIRE grant identifiers for these grants or use the correct format that Zenodo expects.

For the ERC grant, I should use the funder DOI paired with the grant number like `"10.13039/501100000781::101045376"`. The DFG entry is trickier since there's no specific grant number provided. The safest approach is probably to remove the grants field entirely and work the funding information into the description instead. I'm updating the metadata to remove the DFG grant since it lacks a specific grant number, and I'll move the funding acknowledgment to the notes field instead, keeping only the ERC grant with its proper identifier format.

